    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_text">Mimic %1$s. Everything stays on the phone. The internet is only for the catalogue search and the weather. Font m6x11 by Daniel Linssen.</string>
    <string name="source">Source code</string>
    <string name="ob_1">Hi. I\'m a mimic. I live in your room and eat the games you finish: from each I take something for myself.</string>
    <string name="ob_1b">Video games, board games, tabletop RPGs: everything you play goes on one shelf. What you bought and haven\'t opened goes in the pile. That\'s normal: I don\'t scold anyone for a pile.</string>
    <string name="ob_2">Three games at most in your hands. When you put one down, tell me where you stopped: the wisp keeps the note.</string>
    <string name="ob_2b">Finished a game? Roll the credits and give it to me. Don\'t know what to play? I\'ll sniff out three from the pile. And once in a while I\'ll dig the oldest box from the bottom.</string>
    <string name="ob_3">One more thing: the window. Which town is outside?</string>
    <string name="ob_3b">Then the window shows that town\'s real sunrise, sunset and weather. You can skip it: the sun will follow your time zone.</string>
    <string name="ob_start">Into the room</string>
